<!--
  hop's GResource manifest — issue #198, re-pointed by issue #253 (design
  refresh, phase 1: identity). Declares the four vendored Geist font files
  under `assets/fonts/` (see that directory's own README.md for their
  provenance, licences, and why exactly these four) so
  `apps/hop-gtk/build.rs` can compile them into one binary blob
  `apps/hop-gtk/src/fonts.rs` embeds and registers with gio at startup.

  Prefix chosen to match `apps/hop-gtk/src/app.rs`'s own `APP_ID`
  ("dev.hop.Launcher"), reverse-DNS-to-path exactly the way GNOME's own
  GResource convention turns an application id into a resource namespace —
  the same translation `gtk::Application`/`gio::Application` themselves use
  for the auto-loaded `<app-id-as-path>.gresource` when one is present next
  to the binary (this crate does not use that auto-load mechanism — see
  `fonts.rs`'s module doc for why an explicit `resources_register_include!`
  was chosen instead — but the same path convention still applies, so a
  resource path is recognizably "this app's", not an arbitrary string).

  `compressed="true"` is not the GResource default (`false`) and is not
  cosmetic: TTF faces compress well under zlib, and that compression is the
  entire reason this issue chose GResource (`glib-compile-resources` +
  `gio::Resource`) over the far simpler `include_bytes!` an earlier draft
  considered — `include_bytes!` has no compression step at all, so it would
  have shipped every face fully uncompressed in the binary. GResource's
  `compressed` flag makes `glib-compile-resources` zlib-deflate each `<file>`
  at build time and gio inflate it back to the original bytes on the first
  `resources_lookup_data` call — transparent to every caller in `fonts.rs`,
  which only ever sees the original, uncompressed font bytes.

  Each `<file>` names a bare filename, not a `fonts/`-prefixed one, and
  `apps/hop-gtk/build.rs` passes `assets/fonts` itself (not `assets`) as
  `--sourcedir` accordingly — confirmed directly, the hard way, before
  settling on this shape: `glib-compile-resources` uses a `<file>` element's
  own text as the resource's sub-path under `prefix` *verbatim*, unless an
  `alias` attribute overrides it, so an earlier draft that named
  `assets` as the sourcedir and wrote `fonts/Geist-Regular.ttf` here (to
  find the file on disk) produced resources at
  `/dev/hop/Launcher/fonts/fonts/Geist-Regular.ttf` — the `fonts/` segment
  doubled, once from `prefix` and once from the `<file>` text — which
  `src/fonts.rs`'s `FACES` table (correctly) does not look up, so every
  lookup failed. Sourcing from `assets/fonts` directly and writing bare
  filenames here is what keeps the resource path exactly
  `/dev/hop/Launcher/fonts/<file>`, matching `FACES` with no doubled segment
  and no `alias` attribute needed to correct one.
-->
<gresources>
  <gresource prefix="/dev/hop/Launcher/fonts">
    <file compressed="true">Geist-Regular.ttf</file>
    <file compressed="true">Geist-Medium.ttf</file>
    <file compressed="true">Geist-SemiBoldPlus.ttf</file>
    <file compressed="true">GeistMono-Medium.ttf</file>
  </gresource>
</gresources>
